{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Reproduction Steps\n1. Push a v* tag (v0.7.0) → release.yml runs.\n2. Build + Publish to PyPI succeed.\n3. The `github_release` job fails in ~6s.\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n- **Expected:** the job creates the GitHub Release for the tag.\n- **Actual:** step fails with `failed to run git: fatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git` (exit 1). GitHub Actions run 28763401143, job \"Create GitHub Release\".\n\n## Root cause\nThe `github_release` job only runs `actions/download-artifact` then `gh release …`. It never runs `actions/checkout`, and sets no `GH_REPO`, so the `gh` CLI has no repository context and tries to infer it from a local git repo that isn't there.\n\n## Fix\nSet `GH_REPO: ${{ github.repository }}` in the step env (lighter than a full checkout; `gh release create/view/edit/upload` and `--generate-notes` all work against the API with GH_REPO set). Introduced by change 314 (ticket f112-6222-e236-4b09).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `.github/workflows/release.yml` `github_release` step sets `GH_REPO: ${{ github.repository }}` (or checks out the repo) so `gh` has repo context.\n- [x] The next tag-triggered release creates the GitHub Release automatically without the git-repository error.\n- [x] v0.7.0 GitHub Release exists and is marked Latest (created as a one-off since PyPI 0.7.0 is immutable and the tag workflow cannot be safely re-run)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786290842000366001,"uuid":"294885ed-0919-4b29-9e9b-2790c82c30f8"}